Text:
This document specifies the form of a design document.
This document is itself a design document.
The 'scope' is the set of design documents that are checked together.

Text:
A design document is a text file whose lines each end with the newline character.
A 'fully empty line' is a line with no character before its newline character.

Text:
A design document is a sequence of sections.
Two sections are separated by one or more fully empty lines.
No line of a section is a fully empty line.
The first line of a section is the 'category line' of that section.

Text:
A comment starts with two consecutive slash characters and ends at the end of its line.
A line starting with a comment is a 'comment line'.
A comment line is not a fully empty line: a comment line does not separate two sections.
The 'content' of a line is the line without its comment and without its newline character.
The rules below ignore comment lines.

Text:
The content of a line is divided into 'tokens' by the space character.

Text:
The content of a category line is exactly one of:
- Text:
- Grammar:
- Well formedness:
- Story N: with N matching [A-Za-z0-9]+; N is the 'name' of the story
- Define H: with H a 'method header'
A section whose category line has any other content is an error.
A method header has the form R.m(a): R matches [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]* and is the 'receiver', m matches [a-z][A-Za-z0-9]* and is the 'method name', a is any text and is the 'arguments'.

Text:
The lines after the category line of a Text section are English text, with no further rule.

Text:
Each line after the category line of a Grammar section is a 'grammar line'.
The first token of a grammar line is an 'uppercase identifier': a token matching [A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*.
The second token of a grammar line is ::=
A grammar line 'defines' the uppercase identifier of its first token: that uppercase identifier is a 'symbol'.
The tokens after ::= are the 'right side' of the grammar line.
All the grammar lines of all the design documents in scope form one grammar.
No two grammar lines in scope define the same symbol.

Text:
Each line after the category line of a Well formedness section is a 'well formedness line'.
The first token of a well formedness line is in
The second token of a well formedness line is a symbol followed by a colon, with nothing between the symbol and the colon.
A grammar line above the well formedness line, in the same design document, defines that symbol.
The well formedness line 'constrains' that symbol.
A text that matches the right side of a symbol, but breaks a well formedness line constraining that symbol, is not an instance of that symbol.
After the second token, each symbol is written verbatim: Project and Projects are two different symbols.

Text:
Each line after the category line of a Story section or of a Define section is a 'story line'.
A story line starts with an uppercase letter followed by a space: that letter is the 'label' of the story line.
No two Story sections in scope have the same name.
Several Define sections in scope may have the same method header: each of those Define sections is one way a call of that method can go.

Text:
A story line is, for example, a condition, an action, or an observed fact.
The story lines of a section happen, or hold, one after the other, in the order of the lines.
A condition holds from its story line until a later story line states a condition contradicting it.
The story lines of a Define section say what a call of the method of its method header does.
